UID:36c616fd3bd6d1f0@fed-register-maine.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
SUMMARY:[Federal Maine-Related] Draft 2026 Marine Mammal Stock Assessment 
 Reports
DESCRIPTION:NMFS reviewed the Alaska\, Atlantic\, and Pacific regional mar
 ine mammal stock assessment reports (SARs) in accordance with the Marine M
 ammal Protection Act (MMPA). SARs for marine mammals in all three regions 
 were revised to include new information. NMFS is soliciting public comment
 s on the draft 2026 SARs. We will consider all comments that are received 
 by the close of the comment period.\nhttps://www.federalregister.gov/docum
 ents/2026/11/20/2026-23682/draft-2026-marine-mammal-stock-assessment-repor
 ts
URL:https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/20/2026-23682/draft-
 2026-marine-mammal-stock-assessment-reports
CATEGORIES:Federal Maine-Related
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6b0dce0da2bb287f@fed-register-maine.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261119
SUMMARY:[Federal Maine-Related] HIPAA Privacy Rule: Changes To Support Coo
 rdinated Care and Individual Engagement and Reduce Regulatory Burdens
DESCRIPTION:The Department of Health and Human Services (HHS or "Departmen
 t") is issuing this final rule to modify the Standards for Privacy of Indi
 vidually Identifiable Health Information ("Privacy Rule") under the Health
  Insurance Portability and Accountability Act of 1996 (HIPAA) and the Heal
 th Information Technology for Economic and Clinical Health (HITECH) Act. T
 hese modifications address standards that may impede the nationwide transi
 tion to value-based health care by limiting or discouraging individual acc
 ess or care coordination and case management or posing other unnecessary b
 urdens. The modifications in this final rule promote the essential sharing
  of individuals' protected health information (PHI) for care coordination 
 and individual engagement while continuing to protect its privacy and secu
 rity.\nhttps://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/19/2026-23429/hip
 aa-privacy-rule-changes-to-support-coordinated-care-and-individual-engagem
 ent-and-reduce
URL:https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/19/2026-23429/hipaa-
 privacy-rule-changes-to-support-coordinated-care-and-individual-engagement
 -and-reduce
CATEGORIES:Federal Maine-Related
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
