BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4c0e1a9bd92f2caa@fed-register-maine.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261112
SUMMARY:[Federal Maine-Related] Rangeland Management
DESCRIPTION:The U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA or Department) propos
 es to amend the regulations governing grazing and livestock use on the Nat
 ional Forest System to modernize grazing administration\, improve clarity\
 , codify existing policy\, and expand opportunities for stewardship and ac
 cess. The proposed amendments would update permit issuance\, eligibility\,
  and qualification provisions\; establish a framework for adaptive respons
 e to drought\, wildfire\, and similar disturbance events\; and expand auth
 orities for stewardship-oriented livestock use\, including adding the abil
 ity to implement stewardship projects (such as outcome-based grazing or ta
 rgeted grazing) under a temporary grazing permit or livestock use permit. 
 The proposed rule would revise grazing fee provisions to ensure consistent
  fee-setting across the national forests in the 16 contiguous Western Stat
 es and the national grasslands\, and establish a surcharge for authorized 
 leasing of livestock by permittees. It would consolidate and renumber exis
 ting sections in subpart A for clarity and make conforming\, technical\, a
 nd administrative updates throughout part 222. The Department invites publ
 ic comment on all aspects of the proposed rule.\nhttps://www.federalregist
 er.gov/documents/2026/11/12/2026-23033/rangeland-management
URL:https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/12/2026-23033/rangel
 and-management
CATEGORIES:Federal Maine-Related
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d57d35ab4ef69ec6@fed-register-maine.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
SUMMARY:[Federal Maine-Related] Proposed Aggregate Production Quotas for S
 chedule I and II Controlled Substances and Assessment of Annual Needs for 
 the List I Chemicals Ephedrine\, Pseudoephedrine\, and Phenylpropanolamine
  for 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA) proposes to establis
 h the 2027 aggregate production quotas for controlled substances in schedu
 les I and II of the Controlled Substances Act (CSA) and the assessment of 
 annual needs for the list I chemicals ephedrine\, pseudoephedrine\, and ph
 enylpropanolamine.\nhttps://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/10/2
 026-22843/proposed-aggregate-production-quotas-for-schedule-i-and-ii-contr
 olled-substances-and-assessment-of
URL:https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/10/2026-22843/propos
 ed-aggregate-production-quotas-for-schedule-i-and-ii-controlled-substances
 -and-assessment-of
CATEGORIES:Federal Maine-Related
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7c1e1a80cd3ec026@fed-register-maine.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
SUMMARY:[Federal Maine-Related] Medicare and Medicaid Programs\; Cutting A
 dministrative Requirements for Excellence in Patient Care
DESCRIPTION:This proposed rule would reform Medicare and Medicaid regulati
 ons deemed obsolete or excessively burdensome on healthcare providers and 
 suppliers\, with the objective of reducing costs\, enhancing flexibility i
 n delivering innovative care\, and streamlining existing regulations. This
  reform seeks to enable healthcare professionals to devote more resources 
 to improving patient care by eliminating or minimizing requirements that i
 mpede quality patient care or that divert resources away from furnishing h
 igh quality patient care.\nhttps://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/
 11/10/2026-22812/medicare-and-medicaid-programs-cutting-administrative-req
 uirements-for-excellence-in-patient-care
URL:https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/10/2026-22812/medica
 re-and-medicaid-programs-cutting-administrative-requirements-for-excellenc
 e-in-patient-care
CATEGORIES:Federal Maine-Related
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:612480be35195f90@fed-register-maine.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:[Federal Maine-Related] Policy Statement on Jurisdiction and Preem
 ption Under the ICC Termination Act
DESCRIPTION:The Surface Transportation Board (STB or Board) is issuing thi
 s policy statement on the scope of its jurisdiction over transportation by
  rail carriers and on preemption of conflicting state and federal laws und
 er the ICC Termination Act of 1995 (ICCTA). The policy statement provides 
 an overview of the Board's jurisdiction and preemption through a review of
  existing legal precedent\, discussing many commonly occurring questions. 
 The Board intends the policy statement to serve as a useful tool for the p
 ublic to review\, in one place\, concise explanations from the Board about
  its jurisdiction and application of preemption\, which the Board anticipa
 tes will reduce confusion and facilitate the efficient resolution of dispu
 tes.\nhttps://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/09/2026-22811/poli
 cy-statement-on-jurisdiction-and-preemption-under-the-icc-termination-act
URL:https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/09/2026-22811/policy
 -statement-on-jurisdiction-and-preemption-under-the-icc-termination-act
CATEGORIES:Federal Maine-Related
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cf1c4faaa1602e93@fed-register-maine.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:[Federal Maine-Related] Calendar Year 2027 Home Health Prospective
  Payment System (HH PPS) Rate Update\; Requirements for the HH Quality Rep
 orting Program and the Expanded HH Value-Based Purchasing Model\; Medicare
  Provider Enrollment\, Durable Medical Equipment (DME)\, and DME\, Prosthe
 tics\, Orthotics\, and Supplies (DMEPOS) Policies
DESCRIPTION:This final rule sets forth routine updates to the Medicare hom
 e health payment rates in accordance with existing statutory and regulator
 y requirements. In addition\, this final rule discusses the behavior adjus
 tments and finalizes a temporary behavior adjustment. It also finalizes th
 e recalibrated case-mix weights and updated functional impairment levels\;
  comorbidity subgroups\; and low-utilization payment adjustment (LUPA) thr
 esholds for CY 2027. Additionally\, this final rule discusses and responds
  to comments on the provision of home health palliative care services and 
 includes a summary of comments received on the request for information (RF
 I) on a home health specific wage index included in the proposed rule. Thi
 s rule also finalizes changes to the Home Health Quality Reporting Program
  (HH QRP) and summarizes potential initiatives to improve alignment betwee
 n the HH QRP and expanded Home Health Value- Based Purchasing (HHVBP) Mode
 l. Lastly\, the rule clarifies the application of the DMEPOS face-to- face
  encounter requirements for the replacement of DMEPOS items\; makes change
 s to the provider and supplier enrollment requirements\; makes changes to 
 implement a DME benefit expansion for infusion pumps and drugs\; and discu
 sses collection of information requirement changes regarding the DMEPOS Co
 mpetitive Bidding Program (CBP) country of origin.\nhttps://www.federalreg
 ister.gov/documents/2026/11/09/2026-22750/calendar-year-2027-home-health-p
 rospective-payment-system-hh-pps-rate-update-requirements-for-the-hh
URL:https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/09/2026-22750/calend
 ar-year-2027-home-health-prospective-payment-system-hh-pps-rate-update-req
 uirements-for-the-hh
CATEGORIES:Federal Maine-Related
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b4a49d0ccf8b0273@fed-register-maine.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:[Federal Maine-Related] Medicare and Medicaid Programs\; CY 2027 P
 ayment Policies Under the Physician Fee Schedule and Other Changes to Part
  B Payment and Coverage Policies\; Medicare Shared Savings Program Require
 ments\; and Medicare Prescription Drug Inflation Rebate Program
DESCRIPTION:This final rule addresses: changes to the physician fee schedu
 le (PFS)\; other changes to Medicare Part B payment policies to ensure tha
 t payment systems are updated to reflect changes in medical practice\, rel
 ative value of services\, and changes in the statute\; codification of est
 ablishment of new policies for: the Medicare Prescription Drug Inflation R
 ebate Program under the Inflation Reduction Act of 2022\; limiting Medicar
 e coverage of certain individuals\; the Ambulatory Specialty Model\; updat
 es to drugs and biological products paid under Part B\; Medicare Shared Sa
 vings Program requirements\; updates to the Quality Payment Program\; upda
 tes to policies for Rural Health Clinics and Federally Qualified Health Ce
 nters\; update to the Ambulance Fee Schedule regulations\; codification of
  the Inflation Reduction Act and Consolidated Appropriations Act\, 2026 pr
 ovisions\; updates to Clinical Laboratory Fee Schedule regulations\; updat
 es to the Medicare Promoting Interoperability Program.\nhttps://www.federa
 lregister.gov/documents/2026/11/09/2026-22743/medicare-and-medicaid-progra
 ms-cy-2027-payment-policies-under-the-physician-fee-schedule-and-other
URL:https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/09/2026-22743/medica
 re-and-medicaid-programs-cy-2027-payment-policies-under-the-physician-fee-
 schedule-and-other
CATEGORIES:Federal Maine-Related
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5f7121b1ab084310@fed-register-maine.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261106
SUMMARY:[Federal Maine-Related] Prohibiting Illegal Discrimination in Regi
 stered Apprenticeship Programs
DESCRIPTION:The Department of Labor (DOL or the Department) is issuing thi
 s final rule to remove the onerous and legally questionable affirmative ac
 tion requirements that were previously imposed by the Department on Regist
 ered Apprenticeship program sponsors. This final rule also streamlines and
  simplifies nondiscrimination obligations for all program sponsors\, while
  clarifying that sponsors are accountable for compliance with Federal and 
 State nondiscrimination protections. It also makes conforming\, technical 
 changes to the Department's regulation that addresses Labor Standards for 
 the Registration of Apprenticeship Programs.\nhttps://www.federalregister.
 gov/documents/2026/11/06/2026-22680/prohibiting-illegal-discrimination-in-
 registered-apprenticeship-programs
URL:https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/06/2026-22680/prohib
 iting-illegal-discrimination-in-registered-apprenticeship-programs
CATEGORIES:Federal Maine-Related
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1c928db4d6654bdb@fed-register-maine.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261105
SUMMARY:[Federal Maine-Related] Air Plan Approval\; District of Columbia\;
  Enhanced Vehicle Emission Inspection and Maintenance (I/M) Program Revisi
 on and Basic I/M Program Certification for Moderate Nonattainment Areas Un
 der the 2015 Ozone NAAQS
DESCRIPTION:The Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) is proposing to appr
 ove a State Implementation Plan (SIP) revision submitted by the District o
 f Columbia (DC\, or the District). This revision incorporates regulatory u
 pdates made to the District's Enhanced motor vehicle emissions inspection 
 and maintenance (I/M) program since the EPA's last SIP approval. The SIP r
 evision also serves to certify that the District's existing Enhanced I/M p
 rogram meets Clean Air Act (CAA) requirements for a Basic I/M program for 
 the District's portion of the Washington\, DC-MD-VA nonattainment area (th
 e Washington nonattainment area) for the 2015 Ozone National Ambient Air Q
 uality Standard (NAAQS).\nhttps://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/1
 1/05/2026-22592/air-plan-approval-district-of-columbia-enhanced-vehicle-em
 ission-inspection-and-maintenance-im
URL:https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/05/2026-22592/air-pl
 an-approval-district-of-columbia-enhanced-vehicle-emission-inspection-and-
 maintenance-im
CATEGORIES:Federal Maine-Related
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
